# ============================================================================
# <project name> .gitignore
#
# [The whole rule, in two sentences]
#   1. **Only two directories stay out of git: `tmp/` and `dist/`.** Everything else goes in.
#   2. If you are about to create a one-off file or directory, **it belongs in `tmp/`**
#      (build output in `dist/`). Do not create temporary things elsewhere and then come back
#      to add an ignore rule -- that is the standard path by which a repo grows garbage.
#
# [What goes in, do not mix these up]
#   In git: specs, reports, review records, supervisor output, screenshots, measurements
#           -> `claude-outputs/` (evidence and material; keep it)
#   Not in git: one-off things produced for packaging / release / deployment / moving files
#           -> `tmp/` (delete it yourself when done)
#
# [Maintenance] Before adding a rule, ask: should this have been in tmp/ or dist/ in the first place?
#   Usually yes -- then change where it is written, do not add a rule.
#   Fewer rules is better; a dead rule pointing at a directory that no longer exists gets
#   **deleted**, not commented out and kept.
# ============================================================================

# ---- the two directories that stay out of git ----
/tmp/
/dist/

# ---- build output ----
# WARNING: **do not write a bare binary name or a bare extension here.** A real incident:
#    a pattern like `myapp-installer*` swallowed the whole source directory
#    `src/<project>/cmd/myapp-installer/`; a bare `myappd` swallowed `cmd/myappd/main.go`;
#    `*.tgz` swallowed two vendored dependencies. Fourteen source files were silently excluded
#    from git with **no symptom at all** -- `git ls-files --others --ignored` was what found it.
# The rule: output always goes to `dist/` (the whole directory is ignored). Separate output from
# source **by location, not by name**.
*.iso
*.iso.part*

# ---- language artifacts (delete whole lines you do not need) ----
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# ---- editor / OS / patch leftovers ----
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*.tmp
*.swp
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml

# ---- local secrets, never in git ----
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*
# <your credential file name>

# Some tools (the Claude desktop app, for one) keep dropping an output directory at the repo root.
# Block it so it does not pollute the root; anything worth keeping goes in `claude-outputs/<seat>/<date>-<topic>/`.
# The guard `ops/verify/check-root.sh` only judges what is in the repo: ignored paths are not reported,
# **but the moment someone commits one it goes red**.
Claude outputs/

# -- the R&D line's experiment directories (ai/RandD/<topic>/lab/<experiment>/) ---------------
# The dependency manifests (package.json / go.mod / requirements.txt) **are committed**; what gets installed is not.
# 🔴 Always write rules **with a path**, never a bare name: a bare-name rule once silently swallowed 14 source files.
# This is an **explicit exception decided in advance** to "only tmp/ and dist/ stay out", not one patched in afterwards.
ai/RandD/*/lab/*/node_modules/
ai/RandD/*/lab/*/venv/
ai/RandD/*/lab/*/.venv/
ai/RandD/*/lab/*/__pycache__/
ai/RandD/*/lab/*/target/
ai/RandD/*/lab/*/.next/
ai/RandD/*/lab/*/dist/
